why: the table names four gaps; two were called small. This closes
  them, or says why the second one is the wrong question.

what: (1) SET-BINDING on the machinery that already merges — facts
  travel through the BUILD too, so a contribution below an
  acquisition is not lost, and `installing(k)` turns the merged fact
  into a capability the body reads. (2) MEMOISATION: not built. In
  this vocabulary a shared dependency is an INPUT (`Db ?=> Module`),
  not an embedded layer, so the diamond ZLayer memoises does not
  arise; what does bite is installing one capability twice, and that
  gets a report — `shadowed` — rather than a silent second instance.

next: thread facts through built, installing, shadowed, tests, docs
